{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1359735-how-do-you-represent-god-in-mage","id":1359735,"title":"how do you represent GOD in mage?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-01-08T09:25:57-08:00","id":1359735,"title":"how do you represent GOD in mage?","content":"Did you ever give identity to God in some of yours stories? how did it go?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12045-lotoiluminado","name":"lotoiluminado","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12045_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-08T10:06:22-08:00","id":1359739,"title":"","content":"I don't. It either makes the monotheist mages objectively right, or objectively wrong, to define the presence of a supreme deity directly.<br /> <br /> What I do, is have beings that might be emanations, or might just be really powerful spirits emulating that because of the belief of all the humans fueling it, such that it remains unclear. Having an old school angelic entity show up, call itself Metatron, and start acting like the mouth of the big G lets you pull lots of narrative threads without getting into answering such a big question conclusively. After all the most hardcore atheist mage still has to tread lightly around a spirit powerful enough to snap its fingers and wipe out the whole PC group in a flash.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-08T11:57:42-08:00","id":1359757,"title":"","content":"Unless I am doing something directly centered on the Lions of Zion or the Knights Templar, in which case it is a matter of the group's faith/theology, it is a non issue, really. For the past twenty odd years, I have treated the Chorus a Gnostic sect who use mundane/real world religions as gateways to their supposed &quot;higher mystical truth&quot; and the Cabal of Pure Thought as totalitarianists who used the Catholic Church as a method and justification for controlling people the same way the Technocracy uses science/technocratism and social conformity. (I've also long house ruled that &quot;True Faith&quot; is an entirely mundane mortal thing that supernaturals don't get; and my rules for such differ greatly from the 5 level magic power version.)<br /> <br /> On the other hand, angels and demons abound, as they are a significant part of Western magical theories and mysticisms.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-09T13:38:41-08:00","id":1359961,"title":"","content":"Clearly, the Storyteller is God Almighty.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1208-grumpy-rpg-reviews","name":"Grumpy RPG Reviews","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1208_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-09T18:57:02-08:00","id":1360022,"title":"","content":"Two data points:<br /> <br /> 1. <b>Mage 20</b> has a section dealing with this very topic on p.486: <i>Essential Divinity, Godheads, and the Adversary</i>. <br /> <br /> 2. <b>Gods and Monsters</b> has an entry for <i>Christ, the Good Shepherd</i> on p.157.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-09T19:14:03-08:00","id":1360026,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1359735-how-do-you-represent-god-in-mage?p=1359739#post1359739\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't. It either makes the monotheist mages objectively right, or objectively wrong, to define the presence of a supreme deity directly.</div> </div> </div> </div>Or possibly both, if there's two of 'em with slightly different beliefs. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-09T22:11:28-08:00","id":1360058,"title":"","content":"A number of d10s from 1 to 10.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-13T19:30:00-08:00","id":1360801,"title":"","content":"If I were ever to run a game of Ascension (Despite my cripplingfear of STing any game), I would opt to portray aspects or interpretations of god as spirits, but have it clear that they are not necessarily the 'real' thing. Sure you can go into the umbria and meet the Father, or the Son, or the Holy Spirit, but you can just as easily find Odin, Zeus, Brahma, and James Bond. Multiples of each, even, for every popular interpretation.<br /> <br /> I feel Mage works best when the universal truth is ultimately ambiguous and partially subjective. All paradigms are correct, as long as you're working from the viewpoint of the people that have them. You can find any number of things that might be god, or that claim to be, but it's ultimately up to the character if they want to accept that any of those things actually are.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Currently Playing:</b> <i>A large, mixed splat game of <b>CofD</b>.</i> <b>As:</b> Seraph du Salomon, Voice on the concordance. Unsubtle man reluctantly participating in the business of Magi. Awakening 2E homebrew <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1338514-house-du-salomon-a-proximus-dynasty?_=1569864567692\" target=\"_blank\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...=1569864567692</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2598-gryphon-s-feather","name":"Gryphon's Feather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2598_3.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"215"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-19T09:19:11-08:00","id":1361909,"title":"","content":"God is what most of my players aspire to be. I really don't worry about the divinity and most of my Mage-games takes place in the past so there are Gods. And if one thinks modern people are pious, one has not read up on the ancient-Greeks.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;I have all the power in the world to give you, and all you have to do is beg&quot; -Nix<br /> <br /> &quot;There's thing about being a vampire, Frank; it takes a long fucking time to learn how do all the cool shit&quot;. -Abigail","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2521-iguazu","name":"Iguazu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2521_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"738"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-19T13:26:48-08:00","id":1361969,"title":"","content":"I've never had anything purporting to be the monotheistic God appear in a game I've run, but I'm sure if I did I would have it manifest as George Burns.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3505-matt-the-bruins-fan","name":"Matt the Bruins fan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3505_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-23T06:36:13-08:00","id":1362870,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Matt the Bruins fan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1359735-how-do-you-represent-god-in-mage?p=1361969#post1361969\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've never had anything purporting to be the monotheistic God appear in a game I've run, but I'm sure if I did I would have it manifest as George Burns.</div> </div> </div> </div>Why do I feel only us old people get the reference","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/987-tuch","name":"Tuch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar987_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-26T13:28:11-08:00","id":1363499,"title":"","content":"I generally just use this guy: <a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Patriarch\" target=\"_blank\">https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Patriarch</a>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/479-damian-may","name":"Damian May","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar479_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-26T13:54:46-08:00","id":1363502,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tuch</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1359735-how-do-you-represent-god-in-mage?p=1362870#post1362870\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why do I feel only us old people get the reference</div> </div> </div> </div>These days, I feel that Morgan Freeman is the more likely go-to.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-26T14:00:28-08:00","id":1363505,"title":"","content":"The problems with the Patriach are that he's steeped in WtA concepts, and ultimately, boring. For mages he's too easy to dismiss as the creation of human belief (the Celestial Chorus would certainly have no problem believing the Gabrielites shaped the Patriarch to halt faith in the One with a dogmatic entity). For taking the concepts around this seriously in play, &quot;smashing the patriarchy,&quot; by giving it a face that you can take on lacks the nuance of actually confronting both social dogma and the value of faith in the Mage metaphysical setting.<br /> <br /> He might be worth using as one entity mages encounter if they go searching for a supreme creator, but he certainly shouldn't be the only one unless we're sitting down to get our power fantasy on and saving the world by beating up symbols of ills (which is, lets be clear, its own sort of fun too).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-26T16:53:56-08:00","id":1363530,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1359735-how-do-you-represent-god-in-mage?p=1363505#post1363505\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The problems with the Patriach are that he's steeped in WtA concepts, and ultimately, boring. For mages he's too easy to dismiss as the creation of human belief (the Celestial Chorus would certainly have no problem believing the Gabrielites shaped the Patriarch to halt faith in the One with a dogmatic entity). For taking the concepts around this seriously in play, &quot;smashing the patriarchy,&quot; by giving it a face that you can take on lacks the nuance of actually confronting both social dogma and the value of faith in the Mage metaphysical setting.<br /> <br /> He might be worth using as one entity mages encounter if they go searching for a supreme creator, but he certainly shouldn't be the only one unless we're sitting down to get our power fantasy on and saving the world by beating up symbols of ills (which is, lets be clear, its own sort of fun too).</div> </div> </div> </div>True. My answer wasn't really 100% serious.<br /> <br /> Though looking at the current state of religion and politics in my country currently......The Patriach certainly looks like all the mainstream depictions of the Abrahamic God we currently see here.<br /> <br /> But yeah, CC are obviously going to have a more nuanced view. Most of my mage chronicles never go above street-level so the ' Nature of God' isn't really an issue that crops up much.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/479-damian-may","name":"Damian May","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar479_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-27T14:36:35-08:00","id":1363680,"title":"","content":"So when you're dealing with the umbra there are 2 distinct experiences a mage can have.<br /> 1 this corresponds exactly to their belief system and presents wonderful options to expand ones faith<br /> And<br /> 2- WTF is this bullshit my holy script never told me about all the goddamn spiders and the thing that eats names or the hungry meteorites or the river that is made of words or the skull pigs. <br /> So you have to decide when your cast seeks out gods if you're trying to challenge or reinforce their views. A hermetic will look to different systems to explain the umbra than the ecstatic or the virtual adept.<br /> What I do is this- when a group enters the umbra I have the characters all roll willpower and filter their experience through that paradigm. If it's a hermetic who wins the roll its sephiroth and Angel's and walking the tarrot. Ecstatics get more nymphs and goatmen and tend to drift towards grecian enviroments.<br /> As for god? Well my take on God- based on the material is that God broke. Way back. Gods not in the house and theres just a couple of mad angels at the wheel.<br /> I show god all the time in my games tho. Every time theres a seeking.<br /> What did you think they meant when they said Avatars are Shards of The One, anyhow?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>there are no bad ideas, just ideas that have not been refined enough","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1608-iamthesweeper","name":"IAmTheSweeper","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1608_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"121"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-08T03:59:04-08:00","id":1366289,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1359735-how-do-you-represent-god-in-mage?p=1359739#post1359739\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't. It either makes the monotheist mages objectively right, or objectively wrong, to define the presence of a supreme deity directly.<br /> <br /> What I do, is have beings that might be emanations, or might just be really powerful spirits emulating that because of the belief of all the humans fueling it, such that it remains unclear. Having an old school angelic entity show up, call itself Metatron, and start acting like the mouth of the big G lets you pull lots of narrative threads without getting into answering such a big question conclusively. After all the most hardcore atheist mage still has to tread lightly around a spirit powerful enough to snap its fingers and wipe out the whole PC group in a flash.</div> </div> </div> </div>This seems like the best way to handle it to me. When I consider the &quot;godlike&quot; capabilities that a master or archmage can achieve in <i>Mage</i>, the even greater power attributed to Oracles, and that players can meet up with god-forms and similarly powerful spirits, it seems to me that any supreme being that might exist would have to be so transcendent that it would be impossible for any direct interaction or objective evidence to be anything less than a complete anticlimax. Either that or it would, by its nature, break the Tellurian. Best to leave the question in the realm of mystery.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">&quot;</span>Explanations exist; they have existed for all time; there is always a well-known solution to every human problem \u2014 neat, plausible, and wrong.<span style=\"font-size:14px\">&quot;<br /> - H.L. Mencken</span></div>","edited":{"userid":467,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/467-bob-the-skull","user":"Bob the Skull","date":". 02-08-2020, 04:03 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/467-bob-the-skull","name":"Bob the Skull","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar467_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"71"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-10T18:06:28-08:00","id":1366896,"title":"","content":"One idea for the creator I've been toying with since reading more of DtF lately is that when God 'struck' the world in retribution for the Fall and humanity picking Lucifer, God might have been 'contaminatd' with the perfection of creation (and the nothingness it was supposed to protect God from) and that he became 'corrupted' in turn - perhaps even shattered. That might explain why (in Hunter and Demon terms) why God (and th angels) seem absent. The angels could either simply have ceased to exist/die (without god to empower them) or perhaps becam psychopomps/anakim (although IIRC the Ascension supplement suggested the psychopomps weren't angels, only a similar class of being) Given that Mage had a premise where avatars are shards of 'god soul' and there's an attempt to re-unify god (one of the possible forms of Ascension I think) and the stuff relating to the Pure ones and the Wyck (which could also tie IMHO to the Nephilim in DtF) you could take a 'God is dead/must rebuild god' angle.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25533-mister_dunpeal","name":"Mister_Dunpeal","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25533_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"308"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-03T07:12:31-07:00","id":1393775,"title":"","content":"In my only gameround where there whas a more or less connection to V20 and W20 the mentor, who is an Archmage that whas already young before Caine founded the first city, talks about that how he whas congratulated by a personal visit of an archangel. Because he whas to unexperienced to save his true love back then that whas terminal ill and asked Caine if he could help her despite every curse it would bring upon her because he would rather have her alive and cursed so he can still help her when he is more experienced and have her with him for the time than lose her now. So when she whas about to reach Golconda GOD sent one of his Arch-Angels to offer her the same option they offered Caine and congratulate them that their love made them overcome the herital sin. To back it up both have True Faith like living Saints because they are sure of Gods existance.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>As I am from Austria I need to clarify two things.<br /> First my native language is german and so please point out if the english I write is broken so I can improve.<br /> Second I do not own VTMV beyond first three books nor any line after M20 Corebook because it is not out there and I wait for the translation.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26160-koronus","name":"Koronus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"366"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-11T13:57:54-07:00","id":1395908,"title":"","content":"I go with a hidden, malevolent demiurge that has trapped the souls of man in material reality. The ascension is about breaking mankind free.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-11T18:40:32-07:00","id":1395948,"title":"","content":"I admit a blasphemous part of me makes the Christian God in Mage to be another Incarnae of Jupiter or Sol-Helios Celestine.<br /> <br /> The Jupiter one represents any and all gods who are patriarchal leadership Sky-Fathers.<br /> <br /> While Sol Helios represents the more justice, illuminating, impersonal force of nebulous GoodTM.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-12T00:16:27-07:00","id":1395978,"title":"","content":"I just gotta say, <i>Gods and Monsters</i> is the only time I have seen an entry for Jesus. I have seen saints, angels, devils, and so on. Coming from an author who is an avowed neo-pagan, I felt that is was a well considered and respectful bit of writing.<br /> To be open, I am a Christian. Greek Orthodox. I try to avoid being too direct about God in any sort of gaming. It works more harmoniously to treat it as a mystery.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25651-marko-markoko","name":"Marko Markoko","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25651_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"123"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}